.agents/
# `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`: an excluded DIRECTORY cannot be re-included further
# down (git never descends into it), so `!.claude/skills/` under `.claude/` silently did
# nothing -- measured 2026-09-21 with `git check-ignore -v`. Excluding the contents
# instead leaves the directory traversable and the negation below actually applies.
.claude/*
# The skills themselves ship. `AGENTS.md` (tracked) points at `.claude/skills/`, and a
# named skill git does not carry is the same trap as a document naming a script that
# does not exist: the next clone gets the pointer and not the file.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
skills-lock.json
.env.local
logs/
*.log
